module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjTwist
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.ChartMonomials

/-!
# The sections of a twist of the structure sheaf over a standard open of projective space

Grade `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` by total degree and twist the structure sheaf of its homogeneous spectrum
by `d`. Over a standard open `D₊(f)` the sections of the twist are, by Tag 01M6, the degree-zero
part of the localization of the shifted module at `f`: the fractions `x / f^n` with `x`
homogeneous of degree `n · deg f + d`.

Suppose `f = Xᵢ · g` with `g` homogeneous of degree `k`, so `deg f = k + 1`. For `0 ≤ d` the
module of sections is then **free of rank one** on the single section `Xᵢ^d`, over the ring
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away 𝒜 f` of functions on `D₊(f)`. Indeed `x / f^n` equals
`(x g^d / f^{n+d}) · Xᵢ^d`, the first factor being a degree-zero fraction, and no nonzero
function on the chart annihilates `Xᵢ^d` because `Xᵢ^d` divides the unit `f^d`.

Two instances matter for the projective line: `f = Xᵢ` (take `g = 1`), where the chart ring is
the affine space `Stacks.SymmetricAway.chartRing R i` of
`Stacks.SymmetricAway.chartAlgEquiv`, and `f = X₀ X₁` (take `g = X₁`), the overlap of the two
standard charts. In the first case, composing with
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistChartSingletonChartRingEquiv` identifies the sections
of `𝒪(d)` over `D₊(Xᵢ)` with the monomial chart
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.twistChart R n d {i}` of the Čech computation. That is the
bridge between the sheaf-theoretic twist and the combinatorial model of its cohomology.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.chartLocalization` — the localization of
  `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` away from `f`, as a module over itself.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistDegreeZero` — the degree-zero part of the
  localization at `f` of the `d`-th shift of `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]`, i.e. the sections of `𝒪(d)` over
  `D₊(f)`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistSections` — those sections as read off the twisting
  sheaf itself.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistGenerator` — the section `Xᵢ^d`.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistCoeff` — the degree-zero fraction
  `x g^d / f^{n+d}` expressing `x / f^n` as a multiple of `Xᵢ^d`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistDegreeZero_eq_span` — for `0 ≤ d` the sections of
  the twist over `D₊(Xᵢ g)` are generated by `Xᵢ^d` over the chart ring.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.toSpanSingleton_twistGenerator_injective` — `Xᵢ^d` is a
  basis: no nonzero function on the chart kills it.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistSectionsEquivAway` — the sections of the twist over
  `D₊(Xᵢ g)` are free of rank one over the chart ring.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistSectionsVariableEquivChartRing` — the case
  `f = Xᵢ`, where the chart ring is an affine space.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistSectionsOverlapEquivAway` — the case `f = Xᵢ Xⱼ`,
  the overlap of two standard charts.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.free_twistChart_singleton` — the one-variable monomial
  chart is a free `R`-module.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistSectionsAddEquivTwistChart` — **the bridge.** For
  `0 ≤ d` the sections of `𝒪(d)` over `D₊(Xᵢ)` are the degree-`d` Laurent monomial chart of the
  Čech computation of the cohomology of `𝒪(d)` on `ℙⁿ_R`.

## Implementation notes

The two sides of the bridge are linear over different rings — the sections over the chart ring,
the monomial chart over `R` — and the chart ring is only isomorphic to, not equal to, the ring of
functions through which `R` acts on the sections. The bridge is therefore stated as an additive
equivalence, with the two linearity statements recorded separately by
`twistSectionsVariableEquivChartRing` and `twistChartSingletonChartRingEquiv`.

Membership in `GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization` quantifies over *some* degree `e` with
`f ∈ 𝒜 e`, not over `e = deg f`. A polynomial is homogeneous of a second degree only if it
vanishes, in which case the denominator `f^n` vanishes for `n ≥ 1` and the fraction is zero; so
the two cases are separated by
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.degree_mul_eq_mul` and
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.mk_eq_zero_of_den_eq_zero` rather than by assuming `R`
nontrivial.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: the identification of sections of a twist over a standard
open is part of tag 01MN, carried by
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf`, and the computation of the cohomology
of `𝒪(d)` on `ℙⁿ` is tag 01XT, which needs the Čech comparison as well as this bridge.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XT)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open MvPolynomial AlgebraicGeometry AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum
open HomogeneousLocalization Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology Stacks.SymmetricAway

universe u v

namespace Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

variable {σ : Type v} {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- The localization of `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` away from `f`, regarded as a module over
`R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]`. The sections of every twist over `D₊(f)` are submodules of it. -/
abbrev chartLocalization (R : Type u) [CommRing R] {σ : Type v} (f : MvPolynomial σ R) :=
  LocalizedModule.Away f (MvPolynomial σ R)

/-- The sections of `𝒪(d)` over the standard open `D₊(f)`, as the degree-zero part of the
localization at `f` of the `d`-th shift of `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]`. -/
abbrev twistDegreeZero (R : Type u) [CommRing R] {σ : Type v} (f : MvPolynomial σ R) (d : ℤ) :
    Submodule (Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f) (chartLocalization R f) :=
  GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization (homogeneousSubmodule σ R)
    (Proj.twistGrading (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) d) f

/-- The sections of the `d`-th twisting sheaf on `Proj R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` over the standard open
`D₊(f)`. -/
abbrev twistSections (R : Type u) [CommRing R] {σ : Type v} (f : MvPolynomial σ R) (d : ℤ) :=
  (Proj.twistingSheaf (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) d).val.obj
    (Opposite.op (ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f))

/-- The section `Xᵢ^d` of `𝒪(d)` over `D₊(f)`, read as a fraction with denominator `1`. -/
def twistGenerator (R : Type u) [CommRing R] {σ : Type v} (f : MvPolynomial σ R) (i : σ)
    (d : ℤ) : chartLocalization R f :=
  LocalizedModule.mk ((X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ^ d.toNat) 1

variable {f g : MvPolynomial σ R} {k : ℕ}

/-- A variable times a homogeneous polynomial of degree `k` is homogeneous of degree `k + 1`. -/
theorem factor_mem {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k) (hfac : f = X i * g) :
    f ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R (k + 1) := by
  rw [hfac, Nat.add_comm]
  exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one i) hg

/-- A degree-zero fraction of the chart ring, read in the ordinary localization. -/
theorem val_awayMk {e : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R e) (m : ℕ)
    (p : MvPolynomial σ R) (hp : p ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R (m • e)) :
    (Away.mk (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) hf m p hp).val =
      Localization.mk p (⟨f ^ m, m, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers f) := rfl

/-- A fraction whose denominator vanishes is zero. -/
theorem mk_eq_zero_of_den_eq_zero (f : MvPolynomial σ R) {n : ℕ} (x : MvPolynomial σ R)
    (hn : f ^ n = 0) (hmem : f ^ n ∈ Submonoid.powers f) :
    LocalizedModule.mk x ⟨f ^ n, hmem⟩ = (0 : chartLocalization R f) := by
  rw [← LocalizedModule.zero_mk 1]
  exact LocalizedModule.mk_eq.2 ⟨⟨f ^ n, hmem⟩, by simp [hn]⟩

/-- **A polynomial has only one degree, unless its powers vanish.** If `f` is homogeneous of
degrees `e` and `e'` and `f^n ≠ 0`, then `n * e' = n * e`: either `n = 0`, or `f ≠ 0` and
`e' = e`. This is what pins the degree `e'` occurring in the definition of a degree-zero
fraction. -/
theorem degree_mul_eq_mul {e e' n : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R e)
    (hf' : f ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R e') (hn : f ^ n ≠ 0) : n * e' = n * e := by
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with rfl | hpos
  · simp
  · have hzero : f ≠ 0 := fun h => hn (by rw [h, zero_pow hpos.ne'])
    have he : e' = e := MvPolynomial.IsHomogeneous.inj_right
      ((MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 hf')
      ((MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 hf) hzero
    rw [he]

/-- In nonnegative degree `d`, the degree-`n` part of the `d`-th shift of `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` is the
space of homogeneous polynomials of degree `n + d`. -/
theorem mem_twistGrading_natCast_iff {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d) {n : ℕ} {x : MvPolynomial σ R} :
    x ∈ Proj.twistGrading (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) d (n : ℤ) ↔
      x ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R (n + d.toNat) := by
  have hcast : (n : ℤ) + d = ((n + d.toNat : ℕ) : ℤ) := by push_cast; omega
  rw [Proj.twistGrading_apply, hcast, Proj.integerGrading_natCast,
    Proj.mem_homogeneousSubmodule]

/-- The degree appearing in a degree-zero fraction is a natural number once
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.degree_mul_eq_mul` has pinned it. -/
theorem twistGrading_nsmul_eq_natCast {e n m : ℕ} (h : n * e = m) (d : ℤ) :
    Proj.twistGrading (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) d (n • (e : ℤ)) =
      Proj.twistGrading (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) d (m : ℤ) := by
  congr 1
  rw [nsmul_eq_mul, ← Nat.cast_mul, h]

/-- The degree-zero fraction `x g^d / f^{n+d}` which expresses the section `x / f^n` of `𝒪(d)` as
a multiple of `Xᵢ^d`, for `f = Xᵢ g`. -/
def twistCoeff {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k) (hfac : f = X i * g) (d : ℤ)
    {n : ℕ} {x : MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hx : x ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R (n * (k + 1) + d.toNat)) :
    Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f :=
  Away.mk (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) (factor_mem hg hfac) (n + d.toNat)
    (x * g ^ d.toNat) (by
      have hpow : g ^ d.toNat ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R (d.toNat * k) := by
        simpa [Nat.mul_comm] using SetLike.pow_mem_graded d.toNat hg
      have hmul := SetLike.mul_mem_graded hx hpow
      have hidx : n * (k + 1) + d.toNat + d.toNat * k = (n + d.toNat) • (k + 1) := by
        simp only [smul_eq_mul]; ring
      rwa [hidx] at hmul)

/-- **A degree-zero fraction is a chart function times `Xᵢ^d`.** For `f = Xᵢ g`, multiplying the
section `Xᵢ^d` by the degree-zero fraction `x g^d / f^{n+d}` gives the fraction `x / f^n`. -/
theorem smul_twistGenerator {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k) (hfac : f = X i * g)
    (d : ℤ) {n : ℕ} {x : MvPolynomial σ R}
    (hx : x ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R (n * (k + 1) + d.toNat))
    (hmem : f ^ n ∈ Submonoid.powers f) :
    twistCoeff hg hfac d hx • twistGenerator R f i d
      = LocalizedModule.mk x ⟨f ^ n, hmem⟩ := by
  change (twistCoeff hg hfac d hx).val • twistGenerator R f i d = _
  rw [twistCoeff, val_awayMk, twistGenerator, LocalizedModule.mk_smul_mk]
  refine LocalizedModule.mk_eq.2 ⟨1, ?_⟩
  simp only [one_smul, Submonoid.smul_def, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  rw [hfac, mul_pow]
  ring

/-- `Xᵢ^d` is a section of `𝒪(d)` over `D₊(f)`, for `0 ≤ d` and `f = Xᵢ g`. -/
theorem twistGenerator_mem {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k) (hfac : f = X i * g)
    {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d) : twistGenerator R f i d ∈ twistDegreeZero R f d := by
  refine Submodule.subset_span ⟨k + 1, 0, factor_mem hg hfac,
    (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ^ d.toNat, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [twistGrading_nsmul_eq_natCast (e := k + 1) (n := 0) (m := 0) (by simp),
      mem_twistGrading_natCast_iff hd, Nat.zero_add]
    simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded d.toNat (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one (R := R) i)
  · rw [twistGenerator]; congr 1

/-- **The sections of `𝒪(d)` over `D₊(Xᵢ g)` are generated by `Xᵢ^d`.** For `0 ≤ d` every
degree-zero fraction `x / f^n` with `x` homogeneous of degree `n · deg f + d` is a function on
the chart times `Xᵢ^d`. -/
theorem twistDegreeZero_eq_span {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k)
    (hfac : f = X i * g) {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d) :
    twistDegreeZero R f d = Submodule.span (Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f)
      {twistGenerator R f i d} := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (by
    rw [Submodule.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact twistGenerator_mem hg hfac hd)
  rw [twistDegreeZero, GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization, Submodule.span_le]
  rintro z ⟨e, n, hf, x, hx, rfl⟩
  by_cases hn : f ^ n = 0
  · rw [mk_eq_zero_of_den_eq_zero f x hn]
    exact zero_mem _
  · rw [twistGrading_nsmul_eq_natCast (degree_mul_eq_mul (factor_mem hg hfac) hf hn),
      mem_twistGrading_natCast_iff hd] at hx
    exact Submodule.mem_span_singleton.2
      ⟨twistCoeff hg hfac d hx, smul_twistGenerator hg hfac d hx _⟩

/-- **`Xᵢ^d` is a basis of the sections of `𝒪(d)` over `D₊(Xᵢ g)`.** No nonzero function on the
chart annihilates `Xᵢ^d`: a relation `p / f^m · Xᵢ^d = 0` gives `f^t p Xᵢ^d = 0`, and
multiplying by `g^d` turns that into `f^{t+d} p = 0`, which already makes `p / f^m` zero. -/
theorem toSpanSingleton_twistGenerator_injective {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k)
    (hfac : f = X i * g) (d : ℤ) :
    Function.Injective (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton (Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f)
      (chartLocalization R f) (twistGenerator R f i d)) := by
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).2 fun c hc => ?_
  obtain ⟨m, p, hp, hmk⟩ :=
    Away.mk_surjective (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) (factor_mem hg hfac) c
  have hcval : c.val = Localization.mk p (⟨f ^ m, m, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers f) := by
    rw [← hmk]
    exact val_awayMk (factor_mem hg hfac) m p hp
  have hsmul : c • twistGenerator R f i d = LocalizedModule.mk
      (p * (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ^ d.toNat)
      ((⟨f ^ m, m, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers f) * 1) := by
    change c.val • twistGenerator R f i d = _
    rw [hcval, twistGenerator, LocalizedModule.mk_smul_mk, smul_eq_mul]
  rw [LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply, hsmul, ← LocalizedModule.zero_mk 1,
    LocalizedModule.mk_eq] at hc
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := hc
  simp only [Submonoid.smul_def, smul_eq_mul, mul_zero, OneMemClass.coe_one, one_mul] at hu
  have hfd : f ^ d.toNat = (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ^ d.toNat * g ^ d.toNat := by
    rw [hfac, mul_pow]
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [hcval, HomogeneousLocalization.val_zero, ← Localization.mk_zero
    (1 : Submonoid.powers f), Localization.mk_eq_mk_iff, Localization.r_iff_exists]
  refine ⟨u * ⟨f ^ d.toNat, d.toNat, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  simp only [Submonoid.coe_mul, mul_zero, one_mul, OneMemClass.coe_one]
  rw [hfd, show (u : MvPolynomial σ R) * ((X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ^ d.toNat * g ^ d.toNat) * p
    = g ^ d.toNat * ((u : MvPolynomial σ R) * (p * (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ^ d.toNat)) by ring,
    hu, mul_zero]

/-- **The sections of `𝒪(d)` over `D₊(Xᵢ g)` are free of rank one over the chart ring**, for
`0 ≤ d`, on the basis `Xᵢ^d`. -/
def awayEquivTwistDegreeZero {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k) (hfac : f = X i * g)
    {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d) :
    Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f ≃ₗ[Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f]
      twistDegreeZero R f d :=
  (LinearEquiv.ofInjective _ (toSpanSingleton_twistGenerator_injective hg hfac d)).trans
    (LinearEquiv.ofEq _ _ (by
      rw [← LinearMap.span_singleton_eq_range]
      exact (twistDegreeZero_eq_span hg hfac hd).symm))

/-- **The sections of the `d`-th twisting sheaf over the standard open `D₊(Xᵢ g)` are free of
rank one over the chart ring**, for `0 ≤ d`. Tag 01M6 identifies the sections with a degree-zero
localization, and `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections.twistDegreeZero_eq_span` identifies that
with the chart ring times `Xᵢ^d`. -/
def twistSectionsEquivAway {i : σ} (hg : g ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R k) (hfac : f = X i * g)
    {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d) :
    twistSections R f d ≃ₗ[Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f]
      Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f :=
  (Proj.associatedModuleSheafStandardOpenEquiv _ _ (factor_mem hg hfac) k.succ_pos).trans
    (awayEquivTwistDegreeZero hg hfac hd).symm

/-- **The sections of `𝒪(d)` over a standard affine chart `D₊(Xᵢ)` are free of rank one over the
chart ring**, which is the affine space `Stacks.SymmetricAway.chartRing R i`. -/
def twistSectionsVariableEquivChartRing (i : σ) {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d) :
    twistSections R (X i) d ≃ₗ[chartRing R i] chartRing R i :=
  twistSectionsEquivAway (g := 1) (k := 0)
    ((MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_one σ R))
    (mul_one (X i)).symm hd

/-- **The sections of `𝒪(d)` over the overlap `D₊(Xᵢ Xⱼ)` of two standard charts are free of
rank one over the ring of functions on that overlap.** Instantiating `i = 0`, `j = 1` and
`f = X₀ X₁` over `Fin 2` gives the remaining term of the Čech complex of the standard two-chart
cover of `ℙ¹_R`; the basis is `Xᵢ^d`. -/
def twistSectionsOverlapEquivAway {i j : σ} (hfac : f = X i * X j) {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d) :
    twistSections R f d ≃ₗ[Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f]
      Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) f :=
  twistSectionsEquivAway (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one j) hfac hd

/-- The one-variable monomial chart of `𝒪(d)` is a free `R`-module. -/
theorem free_twistChart_singleton (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n : ℕ) (d : ℤ) (i : Fin (n + 1)) :
    Module.Free R (twistChart R n d ({i} : Set (Fin (n + 1)))) :=
  Module.Free.of_equiv (twistChartSingletonEquiv R n d i).symm

/-- **The bridge from the twisting sheaf to the monomial charts of the Čech computation.** For
`0 ≤ d` the sections of `𝒪(d)` over the standard open `D₊(Xᵢ)` of `ℙⁿ_R` are the free `R`-module
on the degree-`d` Laurent monomials of `ℙⁿ_R` which are regular away from `Xᵢ` — the chart
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.twistChart R n d {i}` of the Čech complex of the standard
cover.

Both sides are free of rank one over the chart ring `Stacks.SymmetricAway.chartRing R i`, by
`twistSectionsVariableEquivChartRing` and `twistChartSingletonChartRingEquiv`; those two
statements carry the linearity, and this one composes them. -/
def twistSectionsAddEquivTwistChart (R : Type u) [CommRing R] {n : ℕ} {d : ℤ} (hd : 0 ≤ d)
    (i : Fin (n + 1)) :
    ↥(twistSections R (X i) d) ≃+ ↥(twistChart R n d ({i} : Set (Fin (n + 1)))) :=
  (twistSectionsVariableEquivChartRing (R := R) i hd).toAddEquiv.trans
    (twistChartSingletonChartRingEquiv R n d i).toAddEquiv.symm

end Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.TwistSections

end
